# CBX Shell release approvers — maintainer YubiKey public keys.
#
# Once at least one key is listed here, the updater in builds made from this source refuses any
# update whose latest.json does not carry an approval signed with one of these keys
# in addition to the CI minisign signature. Two kinds of YubiKey keys are accepted:
#
#   GnuPG key on the YubiKey's OpenPGP applet (scripts/setup-gpg-signing.ps1) — the key's
#   Ed25519 public value as exported by `gpg --export-ssh-key <KEYID>!`, prefixed with "openpgp":
#     openpgp ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nz... openpgp:0x0123456789ABCDEF (YubiKey OpenPGP)
#
#   FIDO2 SSH key (scripts/setup-yubikey.ps1; ssh-keygen -Y sign, touch + PIN):
#     sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAAGnNr... cbxshell-release-approver (YubiKey)
#
# Plain software SSH keys are never accepted. Keep e-mail addresses out of this file.
openpgp ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJh30x3wfYCxaZamBHE0i2Gy7npw9+n0EJxR8i8UxjkY openpgp:0x411F3603EC032043 (YubiKey OpenPGP)
